  "question": {
    "text": "The position <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math><i>&nbsp;</i>of a particle with respect to time <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math><i>&nbsp;</i>along the&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-axis is given by&nbsp;<math><mrow><mi>x</mi><mtext> </mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>9</mn><msup> <mi>t</mi> <mn>2</mn> </msup> <mo>−</mo><msup> <mi>t</mi> <mn>3</mn> </msup> </mrow> </math> &nbsp;where <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math><i>&nbsp;</i>is in metres and <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>t</mi></math><i>&nbsp;</i>in second. What will be the position of this particle (in&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math>) when it achieves maximum speed along the positive<i>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>x</mi></math>-</i>direction?"
  },
  "options": [],
  "correct_answer": "54",
  "solution": {
    "text": "<div><p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span>Let us first find speed. </span></p><p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span>Speed, &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>v</mi><mtext> </mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext> </mtext><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>x</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mtext> </mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext> </mtext><mfrac><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>(</mo><mn>9</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>−</mo><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>3</mn></msup><mo>)</mo><mtext> </mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>18</mn><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mi>t</mi><mn>2</mn></msup></math> </span></p><p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span>For maximum speed, using &nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math> </span></p><p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span style=\"position:relative;top:0.0pt\">&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>v</mi></mrow><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">d</mi><mi>t</mi></mrow></mfrac><mtext> </mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>0</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>18</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>t</mi><mtext> </mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>0</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><mi>t</mi><mtext> </mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>3</mn></math> </span><span>,</span></p><p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span>Now finding displacement at that time, we have :</span></p><p align=\"left\" style=\"text-align:left;\"><span style=\"position:relative;top:0.0pt\">&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>⇒</mo><mtext> </mtext><msub><mi>x</mi><mi>max</mi></msub><mtext> </mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>81</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>27</mn><mtext> </mtext><mo>=</mo><mtext> </mtext><mn>54</mn><mtext>&nbsp;</mtext><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">m</mi></math> </span></p></div>"
  }
